    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="0641" n="553" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg553"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23 Repatriates/2</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5241</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-21">February 21, 1933</date>.<lb/>[Received February
                        25.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegram No.
                    33 of February 21, 11 a.m. in regard to the possible repatriation of Colombians
                    in <pb facs="0642" n="554" xml:id="pg554"/> Peru,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d611-f1"
                    /> I have the honor to transmit herewith copies of a telegram sent by the
                    Legation to the American Embassy at Lima at the request of the Colombian Foreign
                        Office.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d611-f2"/></p>
                <p>The Foreign Office in a note to the Legation expresses “fears that its
                    communications with the Embassy of the United States at Lima may be delayed or
                    interrupted” and remarks that “it has no code with which to communicate with
                    said Embassy.” It wishes this Legation to act as transmitting agent for cables
                    between it and the American Embassy at Lima sent in code. The Foreign Office
                    asks that all such telegrams be charged to the account of the Colombian
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
